Q4. Write a NumPy program to sort an along the first, last axis of an array.
Code:
import numpy as np
# Given array
arr1 = np.array([[4, 6],
                [2, 1]])
print("Original array:")
print(arr1)
# Sort along first axis (column-wise)
sorted_first_axis = np.sort(arr1, axis=0)
print("\nSort along the first axis:")
print(sorted_first_axis)
# Sort along last axis (row-wise)
sorted_last_axis = np.sort(arr1, axis=1)
print("\nSort along the last axis:")
print(sorted_last_axis)

Q5. Write a NumPy program to count the occurrence of a specified item in a given NumPy array.
Code:
import numpy as np
# Given array
arr = np.array([10, 20, 20, 20, 20, 0, 20, 30, 30, 30, 0, 0, 20, 20, 0])
print("Original array:")
print(arr)
# Elements to count
elements = [0, 10, 20, 30]
# Count occurrences
counts = [np.count_nonzero(arr == x) for x in elements]
print("Occurrences:", counts)

